From 4b9d5cc22f4c5dc819ecb6455996689413f251d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devon Openheim <devopenm@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 17:28:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [RFC v1 2/2] ARM: dts: asr1826s-kagu: skeleton for
 Ooredoo R291 v2

Minimal board DT applying the asr1802s binding.  Peripheral compatible
strings are RFC placeholders (mrvl,pxa2xx-uart / asr,kagu-*).  The SoC
primitives in asr1802s.dtsi (clock/reset/pinctrl/irqchip/timer) must be
back-filled from vendor sources before a mainline kernel can boot.

Peripherals/addresses/interrupts come from ooredoo_backup/probe
(dmesg, /proc/iomem, /proc/interrupts, /proc/mtd).
